        "title": "Finding the Tangent Line to a Level Curve"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "b652bc17-f344-5009-a0c7-148f214aa2f2",
        ":question/problem": "Given the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+5xy-5x{y}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(3,2).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\u2207f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot \u27e8x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}\u27e9=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(3,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({x}^{2}y+5xy-5x{y}^{2})i+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({x}^{2}y+5xy-5x{y}^{2})j \\\\  & =(2xy+5y-5{y}^{2})i+({x}^{2}+5x-10xy)j \\\\ \u2207\\,f(3,2) & =(2(3)(2)+5(2)-5(2)^{2})i+((3)^{2}+5(3)-10(3)(2))j \\\\  & =2\\,i-36\\,j \\\\  & =\u27e82,-36\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot \u27e8x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}\u27e9 & =0 \\\\ \u2207f(3,2)\\cdot \u27e8x-3,\\,y-2\u27e9 & =0 \\\\ \u27e82,-36\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-3,\\,y-2\u27e9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
